# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- Managed byte buffer standard library (`@std/buffers/buffer.dryad`): bounds-checked allocation, byte read/write/fill, zero-copy slicing over parent buffers, resize, copy, and UTF-8 string conversion via `Buffer_FromString`/`Buffer_AsString`.
- Memory intrinsics (`syscall.alloc_bytes`, `syscall.free_bytes`, `syscall.buffer_get`, `syscall.buffer_set`, `syscall.memcpy`, `syscall.memset`) backed by a bounds-checked `MemoryManager`.
- String intrinsics (`syscall.string_length`, `syscall.string_to_bytes`, `syscall.bytes_to_string`) for UTF-8 bytes <-> string roundtrips.
- Buffer workflow integration tests: file roundtrip, byte manipulation, slice extraction, and example script execution.
- Usage example: `examples/buffer_usage.dryad` (UTF-8 roundtrip, slicing, byte editing).
- Virtual filesystem (`@std/io/vfs.dryad`): MemoryBackend listing and a NativeBackend that reads, writes, removes, lists, and creates directories through filesystem syscalls.
- High-level I/O (`@std/io/file.dryad`) and FileHandle lifecycle (`@std/io/filehandle.dryad`), including append mode.
- Filesystem helpers: `syscall.exists`, `syscall.filesize`, `syscall.readdir`, `syscall.open_read` / `open_write` / `open_append`, `syscall.string_starts_with`, `runtime.object_keys`, `runtime.array_push`.
- Usage example: `examples/file_io_usage.dryad` (native file roundtrip).
- I/O error helpers (`@std/io/io_errors.dryad`), path normalization (`syscall.normalize_path`), and cooperative locks (`@std/io/io_concurrency.dryad`).
- `import { ... } from "@std/..."` module loading with transitive stdlib resolution.
- CLI script execution: `dryad script.dryad`, plus `--help` and `--version`.
- Examples: `examples/io_examples.dryad`; `examples/buffer_usage.dryad` updated for imports.
- Phase 4.1 integration test (`core_foundation_test`).
- POO: `abstract class`, `super`, properties (`readonly`, `abstract readonly`), `interface`/`implements`, semantic validator (`dryad check`).
- LSP foundation: explicit `get`/`set` accessors, multiple diagnostics, parser error recovery, basic type validation (`let x: number = 1`).
- LSP phase 2: inline property accessors (`prop: type { get; set; }` and bodies), `ErrorExpression` AST nodes for resilient parsing, `Diagnostic` with `file:line:col` formatting in `dryad check`, unused-variable warnings, call argument validation, and binary expression type checking.
- `@std/io/stream.dryad` abstract Stream API; `@std/core/disposable.dryad` as real interface.
- `@std/io/README.md` module documentation.

### Fixed
- POSIX compatibility for MSYS2/Windows builds (intrinsic handle width and file open flags).
- Byte-accurate slice semantics in the usage example (UTF-8 multi-byte characters).
- Class method calls now bind `this` when invoking instance methods (`obj.method()`).
- Buffer/file workflow tests use portable `__open_read` / `__open_write` instead of raw POSIX flags.

### Tests
- 31 BufferTest unit cases and 4 BufferWorkflow integration tests added.
- VFS, I/O, and FileHandle tests added (28 unit cases, 2 integration cases).
- Portable `__open_read` / `__open_write` used in buffer/file workflow tests so Linux and Windows share the same flags.
- Suite status: 267/267 passing on Linux (255 unit + 12 integration).
